The Eulerian number \( A(n, m) \) can be computed using the following recurrence relation:
\[
A(n, m) = (n - m) \cdot A(n - 1, m - 1) + (m + 1) \cdot A(n - 1, m)
\]
with the base case:
\[
A(0, 0) = 1, \quad A(n, 0) = 1 \text{ for } n \geq 0, \quad A(n, n - 1) = 1 \text{ for } n \geq 1
\]

I will implement a dynamic programming solution with memoization to compute \( A(n, m) \).

